|ID = 463
|rarity = LR
|name1 = Mighty Kristul Muu
|name2 = Doom Engine Pandora
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Doom Engine Pandora''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mighty Kristul Muu can act as a resilient "base guardian" against Zombie foes in a similar fashion to [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Thermae]] with one knockback and very high stats against them. It guards the base from [[Zang Roo]] and other such threats whilst still being able to reach and kill other non-burrowing Zombies like [[Lord Gravey]], if they get to it, and its fast attack rate allows it to delete many in a short span of time. Its slow movement speed, whilst looking bad at first glance, actually improves its ability as a base guardian as it means it will not stray too far from the base and therefore allow it to catch Zombies that have resurfaced. However, this is not a great trait for general usage, and thus undermines Muu's use as a generalist [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tanker]], making it is outclassed by other tanks in that regard. As one of the few ranged anti-Zombie units, it also serves as a brilliant counter to the likes of [[Cadaver Bear]] and [[Zamelle]], along with its impeccable effective health (1.2m+ at level 50 with all [[Antimatter Fruit]] Treasures maxed) in case it gets into their range.

As a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]], Mighty Kristul Muu has good range, being able to outrange almost all [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave attackers]]. Its Wave Shield, however, is greatly hindered by its movement speed and in some cases, range. It has trouble catching up with the frontline, as such forcing you to lure threats closer, and as its standing range is quite far from the enemies, it may not fully block waves for other units. A good use of Muu's Wave Shield ability would be in stages with the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]], such as in [[Multiversal Studios]], where he can be used to protect your units, especially your backliners from Wave attacks as long as they are a safe distance near him.

Deploying this unit before a boss spawns is a terrible idea, as it will remain far behind the [[Cat Base]] for a while.

