==Trivia==
*Mighty Kristul Muu's name is derived from ''crystal'' and ''mu'', a Japanese word meaning "nothingness" or "zero".
*Doom Engine Pandora is named after the Greek myth of Pandora's box. In the myth, Pandora, was the first human woman, created as Zeus's way of punishing mankind after Prometheus stole fire from Heaven and gave it to them. Cursed with curiosity, Pandora opened a box (or originally a jar) from Zeus that she was instructed never to open, unleashing death, sickness, hatred, etc.; all things bad in the world. By the time she had closed it, there was but one thing left inside: hope.
*The "R.A.I.W" on Doom Engine Pandora stands for Revolutionary Army Iron Wars, a literal translation of [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|Frontline Assault IRON LEGION]]'s Japanese name.
*The helicopter on Doom Engine Pandora shares its design with [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Atlantis Logistix]].
*Excluding immobile cats (such as the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall Cat]]), Mighty Kristul Muu is the slowest Cat Unit in the game, tied with [[Li'l Clops Cat Egg (Special Cat)|Li'l Clops Cat Egg]] and [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]].
*Mighty Kristul Muu is one of the units to have its descriptions rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Wave shield, and High Def./Atk. vs. Zombies" was changed to "Wave Shield, Insane Dmg./Tough vs. Zombies!".
**Prior to Version 14.5, there was also a space between the words "Wave shield" and the comma following it in Doom Engine Pandora's description.

